      "repair_reason": "- [P1] The implementation is review-clean, but an external contributor must supply sufficient real behavior proof before a human merge decision.; Cleared: The revised diff narrows an untrusted-download disk-exhaustion boundary without adding dependencies, permissions, secret access, or new code-execution sources. (sha=382d0edf0de44618bb543060721068da3b874cef)",
      "review_summary": "The PR adds an in-stream 100 MiB byte ceiling to direct skill artifact downloads and aborts oversized transfers before further bytes are written.\n\nPR surface: Source +20. Total +20 across 1 file.\n\nReproducibility: yes. Current main clearly pipelines the guarded response body to a staging file without any byte ceiling, so an oversized or endless response reproduces the resource-consumption condition from source.",
