      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(skills): reject skill downloads exceeding 100 MB",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\n`downloadFile()` streams response body to disk via `pipeline()` without a byte\nlimit. A hostile server can send unbounded data.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nAdded `SKILL_DOWNLOAD_MAX_BYTES` (100 MiB) enforced via a Transform stream\ncounter inside the pipeline. The stream is aborted as soon as the byte limit\nis exceeded — before excess bytes reach disk. The existing `finally` block\ncleans up the temp file.\n\n## User Impact\n\n**Before:** no limit — disk exhaustion possible\n**After:** 100 MiB enforced in-stream, excess bytes never reach disk\n\n## Evidence\n\nBranch: `fix/install-download-maxbytes` | Node: v22.19.0\n\n### In-stream counter proof\n\n1 KB limit, 1.025 KB stream → aborted mid-stream, 0 bytes on disk:\n\n```\nStreamed bytes before abort: 1025\nFile on disk: 0 bytes\nAborted mid-stream: PASS\nDisk protected (0 bytes): PASS\nError: Skill download exceeds 1024 bytes (1025 bytes received)\n```\n\n### Regression tests\n\n```\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/skills/lifecycle/install-download.test.ts\nTest Files  1 passed (1)  Tests  7 passed (7)\n```\n\n### Diff\n\n```\nsrc/skills/lifecycle/install-download.ts | 27 +++++++++++---- (Transform counter)\n```\n\n- [x] I understand what the code does\n- [x] Change is focused and does not mix unrelated concerns",
